Usage:
Helper Functions
isAuthenticated()

Checks whether a valid authenticated session exists.

if (!isAuthenticated(session)) {
  redirect("/login");
}
hasRole()

Checks for one specific role.

if (hasRole(session, "ADMIN")) {
  // Admin-only functionality
}
hasAnyRole()

Checks whether the authenticated user has one of several allowed roles.

const canManageFinance = hasAnyRole(
  session,
  ["ADMIN", "TREASURER"],
);
canAccessRoute()

Determines whether the current user may access a route.

Examples:

canAccessRoute(session);

Returns true for any authenticated user.

canAccessRoute(session, ["ADMIN"]);

Returns true only for administrators.

canAccessRoute(session, [
  "ADMIN",
  "SECRETARY",
]);

Returns true for either role.